* A macro parameter in a character constant ('\1': cmpi.b #'\1',d0) is left for as to substitute
* (it was made the number of the characters \ and 1); a macro with a dot in its name (if.set) is
* called as a macro, its arguments as such (b\2 with eq.s: not a name with a dot); a macro named
* if... isn't a conditional (the epilogue closed one that wasn't open).
* fixed: 0d9517d 2026-10-11 r68togas: quoted macro parameters; dotted macro calls; if... macros
* expect text: 0c00002d 6700fffa 0c800000 61626700 fff00806 00186be8 08060019 6600ffe2
sel.b MACRO
 cmpi.b #'\1',d0
 beq \2
 ENDM
sel.l MACRO
 cmpi.l #'\1',d0
 beq \2
 ENDM
if.set MACRO
 btst #'\1'&31,d6
 b\2 \3
 ENDM
 psect macro_quoted_param,0,0,0,0,0
L sel.b -,L
 sel.l ab,L
 if.set x,mi.s,L
 if.set y,ne,L
 ends
